{"type":"message","id":"d988c8a1","parentId":"cada0e41","timestamp":"2026-05-18T09:09:32.536Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the API key needs to be in the X-API-KEY header. The GET worked with that header. But the POST /send fails with 1101 when using X-API-KEY header.\n\nLet me try GET /send to see if there's a GET method for sending... unlikely but let me check.\n\nActually wait, let me check the method - GET returns data, POST sends data. If I try GET on /send maybe it returns what methods are available, or it could be the worker route is misconfigured.\n\nLet me check if there's a different endpoint for sending. The error 1101 is specifically a Cloudflare Workers error that indicates \"Worker exception\" - meaning the worker code itself threw an unhandled error.\n \nThe 1101 error means the Cloudflare Worker itself is throwing an exception when handling the POST request. Since my GET to /history works fine with the X-API-KEY header, the issue is specifically with how the /send endpoint handles POST requests - the worker code is crashing on that particular route and method combination.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-af46abab-6b38-40c9-b15a-91459a63632d","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if GET /send works\ncurl -s -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration&content=Test\"","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":20732,"output":298,"cacheRead":112,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21142,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779095358157,"responseId":"chatcmpl-185dd94e-040d-4e86-8ff2-2e2119d6feb7"}}
