{"type":"message","id":"29f66a4d","parentId":"737ccce7","timestamp":"2026-05-18T09:10:13.203Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! Python urllib gives 403 Forbidden instead of 500. This suggests the request is reaching the server, which is then blocking it (maybe because of some request validation).Let me try with the `exec` approach, sending raw bytes to avoid any shell quoting or escaping issues. But the curl POST is failing with 500, while Python gives 403 - this is confusing.\n\nLet me try curl with explicit content length or different approach.Actually, wait - 403 from Python but 1101 (500) from curl? They're the same server. Maybe the issue is that curl is sending something different from Python. Or maybe the 1101 is the body of a 403 response that curl is interpreting differently.\n \nThe 1101 error could be a custom response body from the application itself rather than a standard HTTP status, which would explain why curl shows it as plain text and the 403 from Python suggests authentication or permission issues with the request itself.\n\nLet me investigate the worker endpoint more carefully—it might be case-sensitive or require different formatting. I should also try sending a minimal JSON payload without special characters to see if that's what's causing the parsing issues.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-bbe3aad3-fa26-4646-a05a-8e3c44d300c1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with very minimal content\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"OK\"}'","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":1013,"output":342,"cacheRead":20704,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22059,"cost":{"input